WEBVTT

00:01.840 --> 00:07.560
Masshiro na keshiki ni ima sasowarete

00:07.560 --> 00:12.980
Boku wa yuku yo mada minu sekai e

00:19.540 --> 00:22.860
Maigo no mama tabi shiteita

00:22.860 --> 00:25.540
nezumiiro no sora no shita

00:25.540 --> 00:31.840
Higawari no chizu
ikutsumo no yume ga nijinde ita

00:31.840 --> 00:37.960
Itsuka wa sa chippoke na
boku no kono hohaba demo

00:37.960 --> 00:44.040
Ano kumo no mukou made yukeru kana

00:44.180 --> 00:50.200
Tsuyogatte kizutsuita kokoro sukashita you ni

00:50.340 --> 00:57.080
Furidashita amatsubutachi ga
ranhansha kurikaesu

00:57.260 --> 01:02.620
Massugu na hikari ga kousa shite

01:02.840 --> 01:09.340
Yukusaki mo tsugenu mama
dokomademo tsukinukeru

01:09.340 --> 01:15.100
Awai zanzou ryoume ni yakistukete

01:15.100 --> 01:21.300
Kono sora no shita donna toko ni ite mo

01:21.300 --> 01:28.120
Todoku hazu nanda mada minu sekai e

01:28.120 --> 01:30.980

01:35.560 --> 01:39.200
Scar had once again
made an appearance in Central.

01:39.340 --> 01:43.520
Ed and Al worked with Ling to
draw the murderous Ishvalan's attention,

01:43.520 --> 01:45.860
In an effort to lure out the Homunculi.

01:49.700 --> 01:51.220
Their strategy paid off.

01:51.560 --> 01:54.640
Before long, the Homunculi
Wrath and Gluttony appeared.

01:55.560 --> 01:56.540
However...

01:57.840 --> 01:59.100
[SCREAMS]

01:59.380 --> 02:01.100
No! Lan Fan!

02:07.240 --> 02:08.080
Clever.

02:08.620 --> 02:11.000
You took a swipe at me with your kunai.

02:11.340 --> 02:13.000
Can I eat her now?

02:13.000 --> 02:14.220
Just make it quick.

02:23.340 --> 02:26.000
Lan Fan, please stay with me!

02:29.900 --> 02:32.560
If you thought you could
escape from me that easily,

02:32.560 --> 02:35.480
I'm afraid you'll find
you're surely mistaken!

02:40.140 --> 02:42.000
I see you're no stranger to combat.

02:43.540 --> 02:44.160
Ugh!

02:45.700 --> 02:49.580
All this jumping around,
he's trying to stay in my blind spot.

02:51.340 --> 02:52.420
Gluttony!

03:04.400 --> 03:07.000
Excellent.
We should have some privacy in here.

03:07.560 --> 03:10.000
If you don't mind,
I have some questions.

03:11.520 --> 03:13.880
First, I'd like to know who you people are,

03:13.940 --> 03:16.500
and how you found out
what's inside Gluttony.

03:18.220 --> 03:20.500
You're looking for an escape? Even now?

03:20.560 --> 03:22.000
You don't give up, do you?

03:22.220 --> 03:25.920
You might stand a fair chance of getting
away if you'd only abandon the injured girl

03:25.920 --> 03:28.640
because she's just excess
baggage at this point.

03:29.000 --> 03:30.700
Excess baggage?

03:31.760 --> 03:34.140
I can see all those stars on your uniform.

03:34.140 --> 03:35.460
You're the ruler here.

03:35.560 --> 03:38.240
Führer King Bradley, unless I'm mistaken.

03:38.680 --> 03:41.000
A ruler's duty is to his people.

03:41.000 --> 03:43.360
Without them, he is no king at all!

03:44.120 --> 03:47.360
King Bradley, you're no true king.

03:47.500 --> 03:49.000
Not now or ever!

03:49.300 --> 03:50.500
Naive boy.

03:51.140 --> 03:55.000
Don't you understand that there
are no true kings in this world?

03:56.360 --> 03:58.920
[EXPLOSION]
[BRADLEY GROANS]

03:59.000 --> 04:01.000
That oughtta hold him.

04:02.480 --> 04:05.000
Judging by the draft, there's the exit.

04:09.520 --> 04:10.740
Nice try.

04:10.880 --> 04:14.320
But your flash bomb didn't
succeed in blinding this eye.

04:14.920 --> 04:16.120
[GASPS]

04:22.620 --> 04:23.520
Winry.

04:25.200 --> 04:27.000
We won't be away too long.

04:27.000 --> 04:28.680
You be a good little girl, okay?

04:28.720 --> 04:30.480
Take care of things while we're gone.

04:46.980 --> 04:47.780
Winry?

04:50.220 --> 04:50.960
Huh?

04:52.240 --> 04:53.260
Here we are.

05:21.800 --> 05:25.640
Watching Mr. Hughes leave that day
was like the last time I saw Mom and Dad.

05:26.100 --> 05:28.380
Just their backs as they walked away.

05:29.160 --> 05:31.920
You'll come and visit
once in a while, won't you?

05:35.160 --> 05:38.560
After all, we wouldn't want
him to get lonesome here.

05:39.860 --> 05:41.680
Yes, of course I will.

06:07.580 --> 06:09.500
I hear the Elrics are wreaking havoc.

06:09.580 --> 06:11.000
What? Again?

06:11.540 --> 06:14.000
The MPs have been
running around like crazy.

06:15.820 --> 06:17.300
They're in another fight?

06:18.120 --> 06:19.000
Good grief.

06:19.000 --> 06:22.200
It seems they're after that guy
who's been killing off state alchemists.

06:22.540 --> 06:24.480
Seriously? They haven't caught him yet?

06:24.500 --> 06:26.760
What is the military waiting for?

06:32.400 --> 06:35.000
No. Not again, please!

06:38.560 --> 06:39.640
Ah!

06:51.000 --> 06:52.360
It's a dead end!

06:52.780 --> 06:54.420
Damn! What now?!

07:07.100 --> 07:09.400
Nice one, brother!
Appreciate it!

07:09.400 --> 07:11.420
We need to get out of here now!

07:11.440 --> 07:12.700
Permission to fire?

07:12.700 --> 07:13.400
Not yet.

07:13.420 --> 07:15.060
Why the hell not?

07:23.240 --> 07:25.700
Ling hasn't fired the signal flare yet.

07:26.120 --> 07:27.700
And brother's getting tired.

07:28.000 --> 07:30.000
I have to buy us some time.

07:31.660 --> 07:32.640
Scar!

07:32.720 --> 07:35.500
You say you believe that
alchemists have defied God.

07:35.500 --> 07:37.200
Isn't that hypocritical?

07:37.420 --> 07:39.320
You use alchemy just like we do.

07:39.740 --> 07:42.040
I explained it when we met in East City.

07:42.120 --> 07:43.040
It's balance.

07:43.040 --> 07:45.500
Where there are creators,
there must be a destroyer.

07:45.500 --> 07:46.840
That's a lie!

07:48.800 --> 07:52.020
You're using the name of
your god to justify murder!

07:52.120 --> 07:54.240
Revenge is all you care about.

07:55.780 --> 07:58.280
When you killed Shou Tucker and Nina...

07:58.440 --> 08:02.040
I suppose you believe you
were doing God's work then, too!

08:02.160 --> 08:03.340
Interesting.

08:03.940 --> 08:06.980
You two saw that abomination
as well, did you?

08:07.380 --> 08:09.900
Alchemy created that tragic creature.

08:10.280 --> 08:14.220
So that's the science you
would spend your lives following?

08:14.800 --> 08:16.300
Look at your brother!

08:16.500 --> 08:19.640
He's the result of messing
around with somebody's life!

08:20.680 --> 08:23.500
That chimera was made
because a man thought he could

08:23.500 --> 08:26.500
create when creation is
the province of God alone.

08:26.500 --> 08:27.500
[GASP]

08:27.820 --> 08:29.080
Maybe you're right.

08:29.240 --> 08:30.700
But why did you have to kill her?

08:30.860 --> 08:33.220
You stole what little life she had left!

08:33.960 --> 08:36.620
Foolish as you are, you must
still have known that chimera...

08:36.800 --> 08:38.500
could never have returned
to her human state.

08:39.120 --> 08:40.440
[GASPS]

08:41.760 --> 08:45.020
It would have lived out its
life as a laboratory specimen.

08:45.220 --> 08:49.760
Treated as a test subject,
but never again as a human being.

08:55.520 --> 08:56.540
He's right.

08:57.260 --> 09:01.160
Even then, we knew that Nina
would be sent off to live in a laboratory.

09:01.460 --> 09:04.320
We knew full well what would happen to her.

09:04.980 --> 09:06.560
We didn't wanna think about it.

09:06.780 --> 09:08.480
We knew there was no hope.

09:08.960 --> 09:10.500
So we did nothing.

09:11.300 --> 09:12.260
Nothing.

09:12.300 --> 09:15.040
[FOOTSTEPS]

09:26.420 --> 09:29.840
It's true. State Alchemists have
made some serious mistakes

09:31.420 --> 09:32.780
But despite what you think,

09:32.780 --> 09:34.740
that doesn't make
what you're doing right.

09:34.760 --> 09:36.340
And we can't let you continue!

09:39.500 --> 09:41.500
You're so self-righteous.

09:41.820 --> 09:45.020
But do you remember two
Amestrian doctors named Rockbell?

09:47.300 --> 09:49.580
The order came down
to end the uprising and

09:49.580 --> 09:51.840
exterminate Ishval,
but that didn't stop them.

09:51.860 --> 09:54.680
They kept right on helping your people!

09:56.000 --> 09:57.020
Wait, brother!

09:57.020 --> 09:58.360
Don't you remember them?

09:58.440 --> 10:01.500
Those doctors saved your
life, and you killed them!

10:05.620 --> 10:06.640
Brother!

10:11.140 --> 10:12.780
What are you talking about, Ed?

10:13.860 --> 10:15.020
Winry, I...

10:16.840 --> 10:20.120
You mean he's the man...
who killed them?

10:20.720 --> 10:21.920
My parents?

10:22.840 --> 10:23.880
He killed them?

10:25.280 --> 10:27.080
What's worse...

10:27.080 --> 10:29.040
They helped save you...

10:29.780 --> 10:31.340
And you killed them.

10:35.800 --> 10:37.320
Why did you?

10:38.500 --> 10:40.200
They were my mom and dad.

10:40.200 --> 10:41.880
What did they ever do to you?

10:42.880 --> 10:44.460
They were doctors.

10:44.900 --> 10:46.220
They helped people.

10:46.640 --> 10:48.460
They didn't deserve to die!

10:48.860 --> 10:49.860
[SOBS]

10:50.820 --> 10:52.040
Give them back!

10:52.620 --> 10:56.000
Give me back my mom and dad, you monster!

10:56.580 --> 10:58.800
[SOBBING]

11:08.060 --> 11:10.120
Winry, hold on...

11:10.500 --> 11:11.500
You can't.

11:11.740 --> 11:13.040
Don't do this.

11:13.080 --> 11:14.100
Winry!

11:14.500 --> 11:15.600
Don't do it!

11:18.680 --> 11:20.620
I know the animosity you feel,

11:20.720 --> 11:25.180
but your vengeance will only
sow the seeds of further violence.

11:25.500 --> 11:30.980
What you're doing is senseless revenge, and
it's feeding a fruitless cycle of death.

11:31.000 --> 11:34.240
You must end this cycle once and for all.

11:34.500 --> 11:36.100
Fullmetal Alchemist.

11:38.200 --> 11:39.800
Fullmetal Alchemist.

11:42.200 --> 11:44.580
This girl is the doctors' daughter.?

11:47.020 --> 11:48.020
You have the right.

11:48.020 --> 11:50.280
Shooting me would be justified.

11:56.860 --> 11:57.880
Brother!

11:58.500 --> 11:59.880
Brother!

12:01.300 --> 12:02.100
Listen.

12:02.100 --> 12:04.220
The armed forces have almost arrived.

12:04.360 --> 12:06.500
This is no time to be
looking at your notes.

12:06.500 --> 12:08.500
Just a minute more. I'm almost there.

12:09.880 --> 12:11.580
What are those tattoos for?

12:11.860 --> 12:13.220
Oh, these things?

12:13.500 --> 12:18.500
The basis of alchemy is understanding
deconstruction, and reconstruction.

12:19.100 --> 12:21.060
My right arm deconstructs.

12:21.080 --> 12:23.280
My left arm reconstructs.

12:23.820 --> 12:28.140
I studied the alkahestry they use in the
East and then added my own touches.

12:28.400 --> 12:30.800
I discovered something else in my research.

12:31.500 --> 12:33.760
The alchemy of this land is quite unusual.

12:33.880 --> 12:36.280
None of that stuff matters anymore,
didn't you hear me?

12:36.300 --> 12:37.320
The army is here!

12:37.320 --> 12:38.120
Stop.

12:41.020 --> 12:42.140
Why are you interfering?

12:42.140 --> 12:43.780
We have to get away from here now!

12:43.780 --> 12:45.680
Please, calm down and listen.

12:46.240 --> 12:50.180
Your brother's alchemy might be
the only way we have of saving Ishval.

12:50.500 --> 12:51.500
What?

12:51.820 --> 12:52.980
You must have heard.

12:53.180 --> 12:55.240
The enemy has State Alchemists.

12:55.500 --> 12:56.500
They're weapons.

12:56.780 --> 13:00.440
Using their dirty magic to cut a path
of destruction through the country.

13:00.500 --> 13:03.500
Even though we're
Amestrian citizens just like them.

13:04.340 --> 13:06.500
I've heard all about the military dogs.

13:07.660 --> 13:09.980
But what do they have to do
with my brother's research?

13:09.980 --> 13:13.780
Your brother is the only one who
can stand against the State Alchemists.

13:14.020 --> 13:18.420
If he can match their power with his,
he could find a way to annihilate the military.

13:18.420 --> 13:20.580
The threat to us would be ended!

13:22.800 --> 13:24.940
Kill them before they can kill us.

13:24.940 --> 13:26.020
Take them down.

13:26.020 --> 13:28.120
With alchemy, we'll beat
them at their own game.

13:28.120 --> 13:29.980
Pay them back in blood.

13:32.240 --> 13:33.840
Do you see this, brother?

13:34.260 --> 13:36.940
This is the science that you
would spend your life following.

13:36.960 --> 13:40.500
You may think it's for the greater good,
that it could help our people.

13:42.720 --> 13:45.300
You don't even see
the evil you're creating!

13:48.580 --> 13:49.640
Run!

13:52.060 --> 13:56.320
[SCREAMS AND MARCHING]

14:19.680 --> 14:21.940
So this is your alchemy, brother?

14:23.740 --> 14:25.940
[LAUGHING]

14:33.360 --> 14:35.040
This is the great power?

14:35.060 --> 14:37.140
This is going to save our people?

14:51.820 --> 14:55.000
This science causes nothing
but destruction and slaughter.

14:55.140 --> 14:56.740
It can't save us.

15:02.080 --> 15:03.400
Oh, no!

15:08.340 --> 15:10.660
Father! Mother!

15:11.960 --> 15:13.000
Are you all right?

15:13.060 --> 15:14.480
Yes, we're both okay.

15:14.540 --> 15:18.100
Luckily, we were already prepared to flee
from here in case we needed to.

15:18.440 --> 15:19.700
Sorry I'm late.

15:19.860 --> 15:22.500
There were some important
notes I needed to compile.

15:22.720 --> 15:23.880
What do you mean?

15:24.280 --> 15:26.280
Here. I want you to hold on to this.

15:26.420 --> 15:27.720
Why? What is it?

15:27.880 --> 15:29.500
These are my research notes.

15:29.560 --> 15:31.540
This is all that I was able to bring.

15:31.720 --> 15:33.300
Take them and get away now.

15:33.320 --> 15:34.420
Hold on a minute—

15:34.420 --> 15:38.140
If anything happens to me, I don't want
my research to have been for nothing.

15:38.300 --> 15:40.800
Why don't you just take
it and run away yourself?

15:41.060 --> 15:43.620
Because you're a warrior
of the Ishvalan people.

15:43.620 --> 15:45.060
You've been well trained.

15:45.800 --> 15:47.000
Let's be honest here,

15:47.000 --> 15:49.540
You're a lot more likely
to survive this than I am.

15:50.420 --> 15:51.580
Just look.

15:52.860 --> 15:54.500
My legs won't stop shaking.

15:56.080 --> 15:57.580
Some big brother.

15:58.340 --> 15:59.700
You will survive.

16:05.140 --> 16:06.900
Is that a soldier?

16:12.300 --> 16:13.740
Look at his hands!

16:13.740 --> 16:15.360
He's a State Alchemist!

16:27.260 --> 16:29.360
Get back!

16:30.120 --> 16:34.880
Ahh!

16:50.660 --> 16:52.440
Stay with me.

16:52.460 --> 16:54.240
Don't you die.

16:59.760 --> 17:00.680
Damn.

17:00.920 --> 17:02.720
I can't stop the bleeding.

17:03.360 --> 17:04.200
His arm...

17:04.680 --> 17:06.640
Where's my brother's arm?

17:06.740 --> 17:08.400
Where is it?

17:10.640 --> 17:11.620
Father...

17:12.360 --> 17:13.760
Mother...

17:14.380 --> 17:15.700
Someone?

17:16.100 --> 17:17.540
Anyone?!

17:27.440 --> 17:28.760
Don't die.

17:28.960 --> 17:30.500
I won't let you.

17:34.080 --> 17:36.060
I have to keep fighting.

17:36.300 --> 17:37.860
Let me go back out there.

17:37.860 --> 17:39.800
No. You're staying right where you are.

17:39.840 --> 17:40.780
That's right.

17:40.800 --> 17:42.860
We didn't treat you just to let you die.

17:42.980 --> 17:45.220
Doctor, you and your
wife should get out of here.

17:45.240 --> 17:47.240
Young man, we're not going anywhere.

17:49.280 --> 17:50.520
Brother...

17:50.520 --> 17:52.860
Get back!

17:53.500 --> 17:54.960
What happened?

17:55.100 --> 17:56.840
Why did you protect me?

17:58.200 --> 17:59.580
Brother?

18:01.500 --> 18:03.920
Anyone who can move on their own, go now.

18:05.780 --> 18:07.000
He's awake!

18:08.800 --> 18:11.200
Don't move or you'll open up your wounds.

18:11.220 --> 18:12.340
Come here.

18:12.340 --> 18:13.820
Dear, come here.

18:15.560 --> 18:18.240
You aren't well enough to
move around on your own yet.

18:18.280 --> 18:20.420
Somebody, get a cart.

18:20.420 --> 18:21.820
Take this man with you.

18:21.820 --> 18:23.500
He needs help.

18:24.460 --> 18:26.580
Brother's tattoos...

18:27.280 --> 18:28.700
You're alive.

18:28.800 --> 18:30.460
Brother, you've made it.

18:33.600 --> 18:35.220
[GASP]

18:36.600 --> 18:38.280
What is going on here?!

18:40.080 --> 18:41.160
Sedatives!

18:41.160 --> 18:43.520
There aren't any more.
We used them all up!

18:51.100 --> 18:53.160
State Alchemist.

18:53.780 --> 18:56.020
Amestrians.

18:56.560 --> 18:58.600
You will pay.

18:58.600 --> 19:00.500
[CRASH]

19:01.980 --> 19:03.760
All of you.

19:03.980 --> 19:06.980
- All of you will pay...
- Doctor Rockbell!

19:07.820 --> 19:09.360
[SCREAMS]

19:41.940 --> 19:43.600
Go on, shoot.

19:44.260 --> 19:45.580
Don't do it, Winry.

19:45.580 --> 19:46.660
Put down the gun.

19:46.700 --> 19:48.620
You know you don't wanna do this.

19:48.760 --> 19:49.740
Winry!

19:49.880 --> 19:51.180
Shoot, girl.

19:51.220 --> 19:53.620
But know, the moment
you pull the trigger,

19:53.620 --> 19:56.020
There's no going back,
you will be my enemy.

19:56.020 --> 19:57.100
Scar!

19:57.160 --> 19:59.880
If you think I'll let you hurt
one hair on her head—

19:59.880 --> 20:01.020
Will you kill me?

20:01.080 --> 20:02.500
That'd be fine with me.

20:02.940 --> 20:06.660
Until one of us dies, boy,
this chain of hatred will continue.

20:07.040 --> 20:08.600
But don't ever forget!

20:08.680 --> 20:10.760
Don't ever forget it was the Amestrians

20:10.760 --> 20:13.060
who first pulled the
trigger during the Civil War.

20:13.260 --> 20:14.940
It was your people!

20:19.160 --> 20:20.960
Winry, don't shoot.

20:20.960 --> 20:23.500
Just put the gun down and get out of here.

20:24.100 --> 20:25.400
Winry!

20:27.000 --> 20:29.760
If you can't shoot, then
do as the boy told you.

20:30.000 --> 20:31.720
You're in my way.

20:35.840 --> 20:38.000
Don't shoot!

20:48.000 --> 20:50.000
Get back!

20:53.260 --> 20:54.680
My brother...

21:09.000 --> 21:11.240
Ed, you idiot, what are you doing?

21:11.340 --> 21:13.140
Both of you will get killed!

21:13.600 --> 21:16.000
Hurry and get Winry somewhere safe.

21:24.000 --> 21:26.000
Winry, let go of the gun.

21:26.740 --> 21:28.500
I couldn't shoot.

21:29.520 --> 21:30.580
I know you couldn't.

21:30.980 --> 21:32.340
And it's okay.

21:32.580 --> 21:33.960
But that man...

21:34.420 --> 21:37.000
You said he's the one
who killed my mom and dad.

21:37.920 --> 21:40.360
He tried to kill you and Al too, Ed.

21:40.740 --> 21:42.020
But I couldn't.

21:42.040 --> 21:43.480
Why not?

21:45.300 --> 21:48.560
Remember in Rush Valley,
you delivered that baby?

21:48.620 --> 21:50.500
You saved two lives.

21:52.220 --> 21:58.280
And you gave me an arm and a leg,
to replace the ones I've lost.

22:00.140 --> 22:01.740
It's your hands.

22:02.460 --> 22:04.000
They weren't meant to kill.

22:05.420 --> 22:07.440
They're meant to give life.

22:09.300 --> 22:10.620
That's why.

22:15.280 --> 22:18.320
[SOBBING]

22:28.860 --> 22:34.400
Let it all out, let it all out

22:34.400 --> 22:38.760
Tsuyogaranakute ii n da ne

22:39.760 --> 22:45.100
Dareka ga kaite'tta

22:45.100 --> 22:51.120
Kabe no rakugaki no hana ga yureru

22:51.580 --> 22:56.820
Jibunrashisa nante, dare mo wakaranai yo

22:56.820 --> 23:02.200
Nagai nagai michi no tochuu
de nakushitari, hirottari, 

